## err.else.4 (ADR 1135): a result with a value handled as a statement. Its value
## is unused; with an `else` block that neither leaves nor gives a fallback, the
## help shows `_ := ... else ...` and no fix is certain.
fn parse(s str) int ! str
    n := s.to_int() else return "not a number: {s}"
    n

fn main()
    parse("x") else e
        print("bad: {e}")
